@host = http://localhost:5276
@gateway = http://localhost:5299

### Log in as the customer (Petra) and paste accessToken below
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "petra@example.com", "password": "Customer123!" }

### Log in as the administrator and paste accessToken below
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@kofi.test", "password": "Admin123!" }

###
@customerToken = PASTE-CUSTOMER-TOKEN
@adminToken = PASTE-ADMIN-TOKEN

# Seeded products keep their ids across restarts: Kolumbie Huila 250 g.
@productId = 7c1e9b42-0f3d-4a6e-8b25-d4f1a9c3e522
# Today or later, as yyyy-MM-dd.
@deliveryDay = REPLACE-WITH-A-DAY
@subscriptionId = REPLACE-WITH-SUBSCRIPTION-ID
@deliveryId = REPLACE-WITH-DELIVERY-ID
@orderId = REPLACE-WITH-ORDER-ID
@paymentId = REPLACE-WITH-PAYMENT-ID
@setupId = REPLACE-WITH-SETUP-ID

### Catalogue
GET {{host}}/products

### The catalogue is paged: page and pageSize (default 20, at most 100)
GET {{host}}/products?page=2&pageSize=5

### Customers
GET {{host}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Subscriptions
GET {{host}}/subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### My subscriptions (as the customer: only Petra's)
GET {{host}}/subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Subscription detail and deliveries
GET {{host}}/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Subscribe (customer): the subscription starts incomplete, nothing is planned or charged yet
POST {{host}}/subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "quantity": 2,
  "intervalDays": 21,
  "firstDeliveryOn": "{{deliveryDay}}"
}

### Already have a saved card? Activate with it straight away (customer)
POST {{host}}/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Or authorise a (different) card: the shop creates a card setup at the provider
### and answers with its page. In a browser you would go to redirectUrl.
POST {{host}}/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/card-setup
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Without a browser: press "Authorise" on the provider's page (saves tok_visa)
POST {{gateway}}/setups/{{setupId}}/approve

### The provider sends the browser back here; the shop asks the provider about
### the setup, keeps the card and activates. A first delivery due today is
### prepared and charged at once.
GET {{host}}/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/card-return?setupId={{setupId}}

### The card all my subscriptions are charged to (customer)
GET {{host}}/payment-card
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Change it: the same authorisation at the provider, then back to /payment-card/return
POST {{host}}/payment-card/setup
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Without a browser: authorise a card that the bank will decline later
POST {{gateway}}/setups/{{setupId}}/approve?token=tok_declined

GET {{host}}/payment-card/return?setupId={{setupId}}

### Prepare one due delivery by hand
POST {{host}}/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/prepare
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Prepare every due delivery — what the daily cron job calls
POST {{host}}/subscriptions/process-due
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Pause
POST {{host}}/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/pause
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Resume
POST {{host}}/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/resume
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nextDeliveryOn": "{{deliveryDay}}"
}

### Skip the next planned delivery
POST {{host}}/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/skip
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Change the plan for future deliveries
PUT {{host}}/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/plan
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "quantity": 1, "intervalDays": 14 }

### Cancel
POST {{host}}/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Orders
GET {{host}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Order detail
GET {{host}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Subscription orders are already paid with the saved card; the
### provider's page lists every payment
GET {{gateway}}/

### Mark the order shipped
POST {{host}}/orders/{{orderId}}/ship
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Update the catalogue price
PUT {{host}}/products/{{productId}}/price
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 20.00 }

### One-off order
POST {{host}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "street": "Botanicka 68a",
  "city": "Brno",
  "zip": "60200",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "quantity": 2 }]
}

### Pay an order (customer): the shop creates a payment at the provider and
### answers with its payment page. In a browser you would go to redirectUrl.
POST {{host}}/orders/{{orderId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Without a browser: press "Pay" on the provider's page
POST {{gateway}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/approve

### The provider sends the browser back here; the shop asks the provider
### for the payment's status before it marks the order paid
GET {{host}}/orders/{{orderId}}/payment-return?paymentId={{paymentId}}

### My order (customer): only your own, anyone else's is 404
GET {{host}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Validation errors use ProblemDetails
POST {{host}}/subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 0, "intervalDays": 0 }
